    T97
        title       Host tests on Story and Fake; the seam harness deleted
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        description
            Flow's own host tests run on Story and Fake only, and `src/host/testing/seam.ts` is deleted.

            **Why now:** moved from @task.V3.T80 in P3 (the user, 2026-11-18, re-plan Q2 B) so P3 closes on
            construction. seam drives the Runtime directly for four host test files (about 2,000 lines) beside Story and
            Fake, with its own store, host and seed copies, against the Epic's "one runtime, one way to run it". T80's
            driver item (Actors R25) moved to the boundary Task.

            **Read first:** @task.V3.T80 (its routed items, in its comments), @review.code-quality-review (section 4),
            @review.code-quality-review-2 (section 5, A7), code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/testing/seam.ts.

            **Risk:** coverage must not drop: port one file at a time, keep every rule each test cites, and keep each
            planted fault caught by its target.

            **Approach:** the routed items, all test tooling, land with the port: the pair sweeps stop once every
            reachable phase is found; lanes and player join the reload sweeps; a coverage test that each public feature
            appears in a fixture; edge values in every fixture's step samples; `Failure.shrinks` counts what its doc
            says; failure words and write salts stop leaking across dropped fixtures; generate.ts's placeholders (2g)
            and sweep.ts's booleans (2h); Fake's `Batch` stores no derived status (2i); the test clock's settle is not
            quadratic (3g); `buildRuntime` split once the test-only `admit` hook is gone (5f, widening May change to
            `src/core`); and the harness items routed from @task.V3.T29 (2026-11-18T19:14): a reload variant that skips
            keeps the breaches it recorded first (`sweep.ts`), `skipBound` checks that skips fall inside the window
            positions (`sweep.ts`), fake servers honour idempotency keys (`shop.ts`, sign-in `auth.ts`, player
            `speaker.ts`), quieting counts machine timers (`generate.ts`), `disposeRuntime` keeps its Exit (`run.ts`),
            each with a planted fault that targets the harness.

            May change: `src/host/testing/`, `src/host/*.test.ts`, `src/core/` (5f only), `tests/`. Evidence: this
            Task's comments.

            False pass: a ported test that no longer reaches the rule it cites → caught by `nub run faults --only` on
            each ported file's faults, before and after, with the same faults caught.
        acceptance
