    T105
        title       Start order stated as a rule; T102's routed checks built; computed Flow.initial removed
        status      done
        priority    medium
        description
            Start order becomes a stated rule, computed `Flow.initial` is removed, and the checks routed here from T102,
            T104 and the rules pass are built, each red first.

            **Why now:** T102's close review showed start order is observable (reversing it changes
            `BlockedByDependents`' message order and swaps consumers' context-update turns) yet no Spec rule says so,
            and a fault reversing it passed the whole suite. T104's two close reviews routed holes older than T104 here
            (this Task's comments), and the user banned computed `Flow.initial` (2026-11-20).

            **Read first:** @task.V3.T102 (its close review), @task.V3.T104 (its two close reviews),
            @spec.Actors, @spec.Compile.

            **Risk:** Pending D2 (@plan.Machines.O3), D3 (@plan.Runtime.O6) and D4 (@plan.Operations.O3) are pinned here
            with Stories; merging them into the Plans is a Plan edit and waits for the user's yes. T107 also touches
            `src/core/turn.ts` and the context code; its last fix (Turn R22) may land between this Task's commits, so
            rebase nothing and commit by explicit path.

            **Approach:** add a proposed Actors rule (consumers of a wave, a provider's dependents, dispose among peers
            and graces go in start order) with a `specs.log` note; pin `cartFirst` in `store.test.ts` so the
            `start-order-reversed` fault is caught; build the mail-between-items test (removing `tx.followNone()` in
            `serve.ts` must fail a test); close `no-tag-chain`'s `[...].includes(x._tag)` and early-return gaps with
            plants; fix the two stale texts (`SAVED_DELIVERY`'s comment, `FLOW-STATE.md`'s file-level disable claim);
            replace `lanes.ts`'s `id: ""` report with an Option or a tagged no-lane case.

            May change: `packages/flow-state-v3/src/`, `tests/`, `tools/flow-state-lint/`,
            `tools/lint-bomb/FLOW-STATE.md`, @spec.Actors with a `specs.log` note. Evidence: this Task's comments.
        acceptance
            - The start-order rule is in Actors (proposed), and each of its orderings (a provider's dependents, a wave's
              consumers, graces, disposal) is pinned by a named test that catches its own planted fault.
            - `Following` is scoped to each served item by structure, checked by review (no mail between items is
              observable); `no-tag-chain` refuses `.includes(x._tag)` and early-return chains, and `no-id-text` refuses
              renamed bindings, `test`/`exec` and `charCodeAt` on an id, each planted.
            - The two stale texts are fixed and `lanes.ts` reports no lane without an empty-string id.
            - `nub run check`, the suite and `nub run faults --only` on the new faults pass.
            - Computed `Flow.initial` is gone: a function start is a two-sided type error and, untyped,
              InvalidConfiguration at `["memory", field]` (planted fault); `src/flow.ts`'s Computed start, its creation
              step and every fixture, test and docs site are removed or rewritten (a value derived where it is read, or
              an input) (@spec.Compile.R5).
            - Each routed hole in this Task's comments lands as an inverted test titled by its rule, then is fixed or
              left inverted with an owner Task: restored timers in an inactive state; untyped `scope` or `persistence`
              alone; a non-object `updateMemory` return (Turn R10); `generate.ts`'s unknown rule name.
            - T104's follow-ups: `unsettledWrites` takes its rows from the app with no caller parameter (two-sided type
              test); one helper raises `ForeignActorRef` for the Runtime, Story and run; the erased siblings carry the
              app (two-sided tests); `paired-refusals` refuses each hole shape, each a plant in its test first; the two
              stale texts are fixed.
            - @plan.Machines.O3, @plan.Runtime.O6 and @plan.Operations.O3 (Pending D2 to D4) each have a Story that pins
              the decided outcome; any gap lands red, then fixed.
            - Stress runs and generated Stories over fresh seeds pass at close.
