            applier `apply` with rows C1 to C7, the alarm heap with `tick` and the one host wake, the mailbox and the
            index layer.

            **Why now:** fragments (@task.V3.T109), emits and the operations Tasks all write through `apply` and
            `tx.alarms`; the user placed this Task before T109 (@proposal.spec-handover).

            **Read first:** @proposal.algo-resolutions sections 1.2 and 2 (C1, C3, C4, C6);
            @proposal.algo-turn; @proposal.spec-turn-parts.

            **Risk:** the design's model covers part of the text (@proposal.algo-resolutions hole 1); the unchecked
            invariants are this Task's first failing checks.
        acceptance
            - A package sequence test checks I5, I7, I9, I12, I13 and I15 to I17 of @proposal.algo-turn section 8,
              red first.
            - `tick` dispatches the six alarm kinds by a total match; a planted seventh kind does not compile.
