    T121
        title       Operation endings and the retry guards
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T119, @T92]
        description
            Build an operation's endings: the row and its refusal, the head's one unknown, the timeout rule, the issue
            view over endings, and the retry guards read through one `laneView`.

            **Why now:** one of the four parts of @task.V3.T21 (@proposal.spec-handover); the guards `O.x.idle` and
            `O.x.retryable` read lane state that the records and operations designs restructure, and five fixtures
            use them.

            **Read first:** @proposal.algo-resolutions sections 1.4 (O1, O2, O3) and 2 (C3); @proposal.algo-operations
            sections 6.5, 6.7 and 6.8; @proposal.algo-records section 6.6; code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/turn.ts.

            **Risk:** the lane policies (`latest`, `serialize`, `cancel`, `reject`) are in no design; their Spec is
            written from the code (@proposal.algo-resolutions hole 5).
        acceptance
            - Ending mappers receive `(value, { input, key })`, inferred from the contract with no annotation in
              any fixture.
            - `idle` and `retryable` read `laneView` at the part's subject; the faults `guard-reads-other-subject` and
              `retryable-ignores-count` are caught.
            - A mapper that throws refuses its row's turn; the row is tried once more and then kept with its issue.
            - Each new rule has a planted fault that `nub run faults` catches.

